lklfuse: tier2file=, the second device of an APFS Fusion container

lklfuse adds the file (or /dev/fd/N descriptor) as a second disk, read-only, makes a node for it in LKL's root,
and passes it to the filesystem as tier2=, the option linux-apfs-rw reads a Fusion container's second device by.

